{"name":"Belgian Waffle","hex":"#f3dfb6","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"waffle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flat pastry pressed with a grid pattern, often eaten hot with butter and/or honey or syrup.","In full potato waffle: a savoury flat potato cake with the same kind of grid pattern."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To smash (something)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waffle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Belgian waffle","blocks":[{"text":"In English-speaking countries, Belgian waffles are a variety of waffle with a lighter batter, larger squares, and deeper pockets than North American waffles. Belgian waffles were originally leavened with yeast, but baking powder is now often used. They are often eaten as a breakfast food; toppings vary from whipped cream, confectioners' sugar, soft fruit, and chocolate spread, to syrup and butter or margarine. They may also be served with vanilla ice cream and fresh fruit as a dessert."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Waffle_with_strawberries_and_confectioner%27s_sugar.jpg/330px-Waffle_with_strawberries_and_confectioner%27s_sugar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Belgian_waffle"},{"title":"Waffle","blocks":[{"text":"A waffle is a dish made from usually leavened batter or dough that is cooked between two plates that are patterned to give a characteristic size, shape, and surface impression. There are many variations based on the type of waffle iron and recipe used. Waffles are eaten throughout the world, particularly in Belgium, which has over a dozen regional varieties. Waffles may be made fresh or simply heated after having been commercially baked and packaged fresh or frozen."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/Waffles_with_Strawberries.jpg/330px-Waffles_with_Strawberries.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Waffle"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Worlds_Fair_-_Belgian_Village_%284626896426%29.jpg/500px-Worlds_Fair_-_Belgian_Village_%284626896426%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Worlds_Fair_-_Belgian_Village_%284626896426%29.jpg/500px-Worlds_Fair_-_Belgian_Village_%284626896426%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Belgian Village at the 1964 New York World's Fair, where the waffles were popularized in the U.S.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWorlds_Fair_-_Belgian_Village_(4626896426).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Circle_of_Georg_Flegel_Still_life_with_waffles.jpg/500px-Circle_of_Georg_Flegel_Still_life_with_waffles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Circle_of_Georg_Flegel_Still_life_with_waffles.jpg/1280px-Circle_of_Georg_Flegel_Still_life_with_waffles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Circle_of_Georg_Flegel_Still_life_with_waffles.jpg/500px-Circle_of_Georg_Flegel_Still_life_with_waffles.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Still life with waffles, 17th century","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACircle_of_Georg_Flegel_Still_life_with_waffles.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Fer_a_oublie_detail.jpg/500px-Fer_a_oublie_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Fer_a_oublie_detail.jpg/500px-Fer_a_oublie_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_cam